From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: broadcom: bcm2712-rpi-5-b: add mmc aliases

Without mmc aliases the MMC core numbers the SD card host (sdio1) and the
on-board Wi-Fi SDIO host (sdio2) in probe order. Both controllers probe
in parallel, so the SD card is not guaranteed to be mmc0: when the Wi-Fi
host registers first the card enumerates as mmcblk1, and any consumer of
/dev/mmcblk0 (root= or dm-mod.create= on the kernel command line,
partition rules) waits for a device that never appears.

Pin the SD card host to mmc0 and the Wi-Fi host to mmc1.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: claude-code:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b-ovl-rp1.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b-ovl-rp1.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b-ovl-rp1.dts
index 45d3b5cd7495..5902dc220a77 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b-ovl-rp1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2712-rpi-5-b-ovl-rp1.dts
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 	model = "Raspberry Pi 5";
 
 	aliases {
+		mmc0 = &sdio1;
+		mmc1 = &sdio2;
 		serial10 = &uart10;
 	};
 
